        "text": "\"<b>Christopher Logue (born 1926)</b>\nWanted Good Men.  Poster poem for Eldridge Cleaver\nca. 1968\nPublished by Stone Posters.\nColour screen print\nE.491-1985\n\nPoster poem for the black militant, Eldridge Cleaver (born 1935).  A large part of the image is a silhouette of the Cuban revolutionary Che Guevara (1928-1968).  Having spent most of his life in jail, Cleaver jumped bail in 1968 and fled to Cuba.  From there he went to Algiers, where in 1972 he received a government subsidy and maintained a headquarters for the international section of the Black Revolutionary party, The Black Panthers.\"\n\nText by Julia Bigham"
      }
    ],
